/*!
\page page_stFcsPoint StFcsPoint

\brief Photon point reconstructed from an FCS cluster.

\section fcsPoint_overview Overview

StFcsPoint is the highest-level FCS object, representing a single photon (or
other EM particle) whose shower profile has been fitted to an StFcsCluster.
The position is available in local tower-grid units (x,y) and in global STAR
coordinates (xyz).  The four-momentum is stored for invariant-mass analyses.

\section fcsPoint_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StFcsPoint
\endcode

Stored in \ref page_stFcsCollection "StFcsCollection" and cross-linked to
\ref page_stFcsCluster "StFcsCluster".

\section fcsPoint_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| UShort_t | mDetectorId | Sub-detector ID: 0=ECAL-N, 1=ECAL-S, 2=HCAL-N, 3=HCAL-S, 4=PrsH-N, 5=PrsH-S. |
| Float_t | mEnergy | Fitted photon energy [GeV]. |
| Float_t | mX | Local x-position in tower-grid column units. |
| Float_t | mY | Local y-position in tower-grid row units. |
| Int_t | mNParentClusterPhotons | Number of photons in the parent cluster. |
| StFcsCluster* | mCluster | Parent cluster (non-owning). |
| StLorentzVectorD | mFourMomentum | Photon four-momentum. |
| StThreeVectorD | mXYZ | Photon position in global STAR coordinates [cm]. |

\section fcsPoint_methods Key Methods

- \c detectorId() — sub-detector ID.
- \c energy() — fitted photon energy [GeV].
- \c x(), \c y() — local tower-grid position.
- \c xyz() — global STAR position [cm].
- \c fourMomentum() — photon four-momentum.
- \c cluster() — parent cluster.
- \c parentClusterId(), \c nParentClusterPhotons() — cluster context.
- \c set*() — corresponding setters.
- \c print() — print summary.

\section fcsPoint_seealso See Also

\ref page_stFcsCluster "StFcsCluster",
\ref page_stFcsHit "StFcsHit"
*/
